// spec: stdlib File
// A write that enters a buffer (File.buffered) and fails when it is written out is reported by
// File.close, which closes the handle all the same; without the buffer the write itself would be
// Err, since writes go to the OS before they return. /dev/full accepts the open and refuses every
// write, so this runs on Linux only.
var out = File.buffered(Result.unwrap(File.create("/dev/full")))
println(File.writeLine(out, "lost"))
println(File.close(out))
println(File.writeLine(out, "late") is Err)
println(File.close(out))

// expect
// os: linux
// out: Ok{ value: void }
// out: Err{ error: Error{ message: "write /dev/full: no space left on device" } }
// out: true
// out: Ok{ value: void }
